During the Framing phase, we will work closely with the client to define the project scope, objectives, and key performance indicators. In the Design phase, we will design the AI assistance solution, taking into account the client's requirements for supporting hospital staff in clinical and administrative activities, improving efficiency, and ensuring data sovereignty.

The Pilot phase will involve deploying the solution in one or two departments, with a limited number of users, to test and refine the solution. This will help us identify and address any issues before scaling up to the entire hospital. The Generalisation phase will involve rolling out the solution to all services, with the support of change management and staff training.

Throughout the project, we will ensure that our solution is hosted on a SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure, guaranteeing data sovereignty and compliance with regulatory requirements. Our partner, OuraneCloud, will provide the necessary hosting capabilities.

We will also work closely with Ligeo Santé, our health-IT integrator partner, to ensure seamless integration with the hospital's existing systems, including the electronic patient record (DPI) and hospital information system (SIH).

Our dedicated team, consisting of a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, and security compliance lead, will work collaboratively to deliver the solution. We will provide regular progress updates and ensure that the client is informed and involved throughout the project.

By following this structured approach, we are confident that we can deliver an effective AI assistance solution that meets the client's needs, improves efficiency, and ensures data sovereignty, all within the specified time frame and budget of €900,000 over 5 years.
